    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0442" n="338" xml:id="pg338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/118: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua (Hanna) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-23T11:00:00-05:45">November 23,
                            1932—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>218. My 215, November 18, 2 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d356-f1"/> In an informal
                    conversation with Dr. Sacasa yesterday he gave me to understand that he is
                    definitely opposed to denouncing the 1923 treaties and I have telegraphed
                    Minister Whitehouse accordingly in reply to his telegram requesting Sacasa’s
                    opinion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
